  "updated_at": "2026-06-16T12:42:34Z",
  "body": "\ud83d\udc4b Thanks for opening this issue!\n\nI found a similar issue in our tracker that might address your problem:\n\n_[Issue weaviate/weaviate#11400: flatSearchCutoff accepts negative values (no validation)](https://github.com/weaviate/weaviate/issues/11400)_\n\n_This issue is the closest match because it reports the same class of schema-validation bug: Weaviate accepts a negative configuration value in `vectorIndexConfig` without rejecting it. Like your `desiredCount=-1` case, it concerns an invalid non-positive numeric setting being silently accepted instead of returning a validation error._\n\nPlease check if this is the same issue. If so, consider adding your input there or closing this one. Thanks for helping us keep the issue tracker organized! \ud83d\ude80\n\n---\n<div align=\"center\">\n<img src=\"https://tse1.mm.bing.net/th/id/OIP.A-2PG7j0L0X0H3M3lHuB4QHaHa\" width=\"32\" height=\"32\" alt=\"Weaviate Logo\">\n<br>\n<sub><strong>Powered by Weaviate</strong></sub>\n</div>",
